## Types and operators

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `int`, `long` (`5L`), `double`, `boolean`, `char` (`'a'`) | Primitives |
| `String s = "text"; var x = 1;` | Reference type; inferred local |
| `final int MAX = 10;` | Constant |
| `(int) 3.9`, `Integer.parseInt("42")`, `String.valueOf(42)` | Conversions |
| `/ %` with ints | Integer division, remainder (`Math.floorMod` for non-negative) |
| `&& \|\| !`, `cond ? a : b` | Logic (short-circuit), conditional |
| `a.equals(b)` | Compare objects' contents (`==` compares references) |

## Strings

| Code | Gives |
|---|---|
| `s.length()`, `s.charAt(i)`, `s.substring(a, b)` | Length, character, part (b excluded) |
| `s.indexOf(x)`, `s.contains(x)`, `s.startsWith(x)` | Search |
| `s.trim()`, `s.toUpperCase()`, `s.replace(a, b)` | New strings |
| `s.split("\\s+")`, `String.join(", ", parts)` | Split, join |
| `s.isBlank()`, `s.equalsIgnoreCase(t)`, `s.compareTo(t)` | Tests and order |
| `new StringBuilder().append(x).reverse().toString()` | Building strings |
| `"%d items".formatted(n)`, `String.format(Locale.ROOT, "%.2f", x)` | Formatting |

